content.text:
The root cause is `ts-route-service`'s database calls, which became slow; I found no other fault that reached users.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-route-service",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'nor' p, span_name, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms, quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95 FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND span_name LIKE 'SELECT%' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'abn', span_name, count(*), avg(duration)/1e6, quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND span_name LIKE 'SELECT%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 2,1",
          "claim": "Route-service SELECT DB spans (ts.route_stations, ts.route_distances, ts.route) went from p95 ~0.1-0.3 ms to ~210-220 ms in the abnormal period."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'nor' p, span_name, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms, quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95 FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND span_name IN ('RouteRepository.findAll','RouteRepository.findById','RouteController.queryAll') GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'abn', span_name, count(*), avg(duration)/1e6, quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND span_name IN ('RouteRepository.findAll','RouteRepository.findById','RouteController.queryAll') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 2,1",
